### #1 🔴 Critical: `NullPropagatedOperands` treats every binary operator as null-propagating, producing silently wrong query results

... Its binary arm applies no operator filter at all:

```csharp
else if (expression is SqlBinaryExpression binary)
{
    NullPropagatedOperands(binary.Left, operands);
    NullPropagatedOperands(binary.Right, operands);
}
```

### #7 🟡 Medium: `func.Instance!` drops the null check its own sibling block performs

```csharp
if (func.InstancePropagatesNullability == true)
{
    NullPropagatedOperands(func.Instance!, operands);
}
```

... The copy dropped the `Instance: not null` half and replaced a pattern with `== true`.
